/-
# O'Meara §82: lattices in a quadratic space (the notions used in Chapter IX)

**Setting.** $R$ is a commutative ring with an algebra map to a field $F$ in which $2$ is invertible; for most
results $R$ is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $F$ (O'Meara's ring $\mathfrak o$ of integers of a
local field, Chapter IX, p. 239). $(V, Q)$ is a quadratic space over $F$ (Mathlib `QuadraticForm F V`) and a
*lattice in $V$* is a finitely generated $R$-submodule $L \subseteq V$ (`Submodule R V`); it is a lattice *on* $V$ when
moreover $FL = V$ (Mathlib's `Submodule.IsLattice F L`).

**Conventions.** O'Meara's symmetric bilinear form $B$ satisfies $B(x, x) = Q(x)$; here $B$ is
`OMeara.bil Q` $=$ Mathlib's `QuadraticMap.associated Q`, i.e. $B(x,y) = \tfrac12\,(Q(x+y) - Q(x) - Q(y))$, half of
Mathlib's polar form. All ideals of $F$ are $R$-submodules of $F$ (`Submodule R F`); $\mathfrak o$ is
`(1 : Submodule R F)`.

**Defines** (O'Meara 1963, §82, pp. 220–238): the scale $\mathfrak sL$ (`scale`), the norm $\mathfrak nL$
(`normIdeal`), the matrix $(B(x_i,x_j))$ of a family (`gram`), the volume $\mathfrak vL$ (`volume`), the
discriminant (`HasDisc`), regular lattices (`IsRegular`), $\mathfrak a$-modular and unimodular lattices
(`IsModular`, `IsUnimodular`), orthogonal splittings $L = L_1 \perp \cdots \perp L_t$ (`IsOrthSplit`) and
$L = J \perp K$ (`IsOrthSum`), the sublattice $L^{\mathfrak a} = \{x \in L : B(x, L) \subseteq \mathfrak a\}$
(`subA`), $\mathfrak a$-maximal lattices (`IsMaximal`), the orthogonal group $O(V)$ (`orth`), the group of units
$O(L)$ (`orthLat`), the class $\operatorname{cls} L$ (`cls`), and isometry of lattices (`IsometricLat`).

**Proves** the facts of §82 used in Chapter IX: $Q(L) \subseteq \mathfrak nL \subseteq \mathfrak sL$ and
$2\,\mathfrak sL \subseteq \mathfrak nL$ (§82E, p. 227), the scale of a lattice from a spanning family (82:8 (1),
p. 227), the volume from a base (§82E, p. 229), the matrix criterion for $\alpha$-modular lattices (82:13, p. 231,
for any scale), and the splitting criterion 82:15 (p. 232) with its corollary 82:15a.
-/
import Mathlib
import QuadFormsKB.Citation

open QuadraticMap Submodule Module
open scoped Matrix

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace QuadFormsKB.OMeara

section Defs

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra R F] [Invertible (2 : F)]
variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [Module R V] [IsScalarTower R F V]
variable (Q : QuadraticForm F V)

/-- **O'Meara's symmetric bilinear form** $B$ of the quadratic space $(V, Q)$ (O'Meara 1963, §41A, p. 84):
$B(x, y) = \tfrac12\,(Q(x+y) - Q(x) - Q(y))$, so that $B(x, x) = Q(x)$. This is Mathlib's
`QuadraticMap.associated Q`, half of the polar form $Q(x+y) - Q(x) - Q(y)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§41A, p. 84 (the bilinear form B with B(x,x) = Q(x))"]
abbrev bil (x y : V) : F := QuadraticMap.associated Q x y

/-- **The scale** $\mathfrak sL$ of a lattice $L$ in $V$ (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 227): the $R$-submodule of $F$
generated by the values $B(x, y)$, $x, y \in L$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 227 (the scale sL)"]
def scale (L : Submodule R V) : Submodule R F :=
  span R (Set.image2 (bil Q) (L : Set V) (L : Set V))

/-- **The norm** $\mathfrak nL$ of a lattice $L$ in $V$ (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 227): the $R$-submodule of $F$
generated by the values $Q(x)$, $x \in L$. (Not to be confused with the norm group $\mathfrak gL$ of §93A.) -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 227 (the norm nL)"]
def normIdeal (L : Submodule R V) : Submodule R F :=
  span R (Q '' (L : Set V))

/-- **The matrix** $(B(x_i, x_j))_{i,j}$ of a family $x = (x_i)_{i \in \iota}$ of vectors of $V$ (O'Meara 1963,
§41B, p. 85; §82B, p. 221: the matrix of a lattice in a base); its determinant is the discriminant
$d(x_1, \dots, x_n)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82B, p. 221 (matrix of a lattice in a base); §41B, p. 85"]
def gram {ι : Type*} (x : ι → V) : Matrix ι ι F :=
  Matrix.of fun i j => bil Q (x i) (x j)

/-- **The volume** $\mathfrak vL$ of a lattice $L$ in $V$ (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 229). O'Meara defines
$\mathfrak vL = \mathfrak a_1^2 \cdots \mathfrak a_r^2\, d(x_1, \dots, x_r)$ for an adapted base
$L = \mathfrak a_1 x_1 + \dots + \mathfrak a_r x_r$, and $\mathfrak v0 = \mathfrak o$. Here, equivalently, $\mathfrak vL$
is the $R$-submodule of $F$ generated by the discriminants $\det(B(x_i, x_j))$ of all $r$-tuples
$x_1, \dots, x_r$ of vectors of $L$, where $r$ is the rank of $L$; for a free lattice this is
$d(x_1, \dots, x_r)\,R$ for any base (`volume_eq_span_det`), and for $L = 0$ it is $R = \mathfrak o$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 229 (the volume vL)"]
def volume (L : Submodule R V) : Submodule R F :=
  span R {d | ∃ x : Fin (finrank R L) → V, (∀ i, x i ∈ L) ∧ (gram Q x).det = d}

/-- **$dL = \beta$** (O'Meara 1963, §82B, p. 222): the lattice $L$ has a base $x_1, \dots, x_r$ with
discriminant $d(x_1, \dots, x_r) = \det(B(x_i, x_j)) = \beta$. (O'Meara's discriminant $dL$ is the class of
$\beta$ in $F/\mathfrak u^2$, well defined since a change of base multiplies $d$ by the square of a unit.) -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82B, p. 222 (the discriminant dL)"]
def HasDisc (L : Submodule R V) (β : F) : Prop :=
  ∃ b : Basis (Fin (finrank R L)) R L, (gram Q fun i => (b i : V)).det = β

/-- **Regular lattice** (O'Meara 1963, §82D, p. 225): the radical $\{x \in L : B(x, L) = 0\}$ is $0$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82D, p. 225 (radical; regular lattice)"]
def IsRegular (L : Submodule R V) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ L, (∀ y ∈ L, bil Q x y = 0) → x = 0

/-- **$\mathfrak a$-modular lattice** (O'Meara 1963, §82G, p. 231): $\mathfrak sL = \mathfrak a$ and
$\mathfrak vL = \mathfrak a^r$, $r$ the rank of $L$, for a fractional ideal $\mathfrak a$ (here: a non-zero
$R$-submodule of $F$). An $\mathfrak a$-modular lattice is non-zero and regular. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, p. 231 (a-modular lattice)"]
def IsModular (a : Submodule R F) (L : Submodule R V) : Prop :=
  a ≠ ⊥ ∧ scale Q L = a ∧ volume Q L = a ^ finrank R L

/-- **Unimodular lattice** (O'Meara 1963, §82G, p. 231): $\mathfrak o$-modular. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, p. 231 (unimodular lattice)"]
def IsUnimodular (L : Submodule R V) : Prop :=
  IsModular Q 1 L

/-- **Orthogonal splitting** $L = L_1 \perp \cdots \perp L_t$ (O'Meara 1963, §82D, p. 224): $L$ is the direct sum
of the sublattices $L_i$ (as $R$-modules: they are independent and generate $L$) and $B(L_i, L_j) = 0$ for
$i \ne j$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82D, p. 224 (orthogonal splitting)"]
structure IsOrthSplit (L : Submodule R V) {ι : Type*} (Ls : ι → Submodule R V) : Prop where
  orth : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → ∀ x ∈ Ls i, ∀ y ∈ Ls j, bil Q x y = 0
  indep : iSupIndep Ls
  iSup_eq : ⨆ i, Ls i = L

/-- **Orthogonal splitting into two components** $L = J \perp K$ (O'Meara 1963, §82D, p. 224):
$L = J \oplus K$ and $B(J, K) = 0$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82D, p. 224 (L = J ⊥ K)"]
structure IsOrthSum (L J K : Submodule R V) : Prop where
  orth : ∀ x ∈ J, ∀ y ∈ K, bil Q x y = 0
  disjoint : Disjoint J K
  sup_eq : J ⊔ K = L

/-- **The sublattice** $L^{\mathfrak a} = \{x \in L : B(x, L) \subseteq \mathfrak a\}$ (O'Meara 1963, §82I,
p. 237). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82I, p. 237 (the lattice L^a)"]
def subA (a : Submodule R F) (L : Submodule R V) : Submodule R V where
  carrier := {x | x ∈ L ∧ ∀ y ∈ L, bil Q x y ∈ a}
  add_mem' := by
    rintro x x' ⟨hx, hx'⟩ ⟨hy, hy'⟩
    refine ⟨L.add_mem hx hy, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    simpa [bil, LinearMap.add_apply] using a.add_mem (hx' z hz) (hy' z hz)
  zero_mem' := ⟨L.zero_mem, fun z _ => by simp [bil]⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c x ⟨hx, hx'⟩
    refine ⟨L.smul_mem c hx, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    have : bil Q (c • x) z = c • bil Q x z := by
      rw [← algebraMap_smul F c x]
      simp [bil, LinearMap.smul_apply, Algebra.smul_def]
    rw [this]
    exact a.smul_mem c (hx' z hz)

/-- **The orthogonal complement of $J$ in $L$**: $\{x \in L : B(x, J) = 0\}$ (O'Meara 1963, §82D, p. 226: if
$L = J \perp K$ with $J$ regular then $K = \{x \in L : B(x, J) = 0\}$). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82D, p. 226 (K = {x ∈ J | B(x, L) = 0})"]
def splitComp (L J : Submodule R V) : Submodule R V where
  carrier := {x | x ∈ L ∧ ∀ z ∈ J, bil Q x z = 0}
  add_mem' := by
    rintro x y ⟨hx, hx'⟩ ⟨hy, hy'⟩
    exact ⟨L.add_mem hx hy, fun z hz => by simp [bil, LinearMap.add_apply, hx' z hz, hy' z hz] at *⟩
  zero_mem' := ⟨L.zero_mem, fun z _ => by simp [bil]⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c x ⟨hx, hx'⟩
    refine ⟨L.smul_mem c hx, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    have := hx' z hz
    rw [← algebraMap_smul F c x]
    simp only [bil] at this ⊢
    simp [this]

/-- **$\mathfrak a$-maximal lattice** (O'Meara 1963, §82H, p. 234): $L$ is a lattice on $V$ with
$\mathfrak nL \subseteq \mathfrak a$, and every lattice $K$ on $V$ with $K \supseteq L$ and
$\mathfrak nK \subseteq \mathfrak a$ equals $L$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82H, p. 234 (a-maximal lattice)"]
def IsMaximal (a : Submodule R F) (L : Submodule R V) : Prop :=
  L.IsLattice F ∧ normIdeal Q L ≤ a ∧
    ∀ K : Submodule R V, K.IsLattice F → L ≤ K → normIdeal Q K ≤ a → K = L

/-- **The orthogonal group** $O(V)$ (O'Meara 1963, §41A, p. 84): the $F$-linear automorphisms $\sigma$ of $V$
with $Q(\sigma x) = Q(x)$. (The same group as `Lattices.orthGroupV`, which is stated over a number field.) -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§41A, p. 84 (orthogonal group O(V))"]
def orth : Subgroup (V ≃ₗ[F] V) where
  carrier := {σ | ∀ x, Q (σ x) = Q x}
  mul_mem' := by
    intro σ τ hσ hτ x
    simp [hσ (τ x), hτ x]
  one_mem' := fun x => rfl
  inv_mem' := by
    intro σ hσ x
    have := hσ (σ⁻¹ x)
    simp only [LinearEquiv.coe_inv] at this ⊢
    rw [← this]; simp

/-- **The image $\sigma L$ of a lattice** under $\sigma \in GL(V)$. -/
abbrev latMap (σ : V ≃ₗ[F] V) (L : Submodule R V) : Submodule R V :=
  L.map ((σ : V →ₗ[F] V).restrictScalars R)

/-- **The group of units** $O(L) = \{\sigma \in O(V) : \sigma L = L\}$ of a lattice $L$ (O'Meara 1963, §82C,
p. 223). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82C, p. 223 (the group of units O(L))"]
def orthLat (L : Submodule R V) : Subgroup (V ≃ₗ[F] V) where
  carrier := {σ | σ ∈ orth Q ∧ latMap σ L = L}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro σ τ ⟨hσ, hσL⟩ ⟨hτ, hτL⟩
    refine ⟨(orth Q).mul_mem hσ hτ, ?_⟩
    have : ((σ * τ : V ≃ₗ[F] V) : V →ₗ[F] V).restrictScalars R =
        ((σ : V →ₗ[F] V).restrictScalars R).comp ((τ : V →ₗ[F] V).restrictScalars R) := rfl
    simp only [latMap] at hσL hτL ⊢
    rw [this, Submodule.map_comp, hτL, hσL]
  one_mem' := ⟨(orth Q).one_mem, by ext x; simp⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro σ ⟨hσ, hσL⟩
    refine ⟨(orth Q).inv_mem hσ, ?_⟩
    conv_lhs => rw [← hσL]
    ext x
    simp only [latMap, Submodule.mem_map, LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars, LinearEquiv.coe_coe]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨y, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      simpa using hz
    · intro hx
      exact ⟨σ x, ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, by simp⟩

/-- **The class** $\operatorname{cls} L$ of a lattice $L$ on $V$ (O'Meara 1963, §82C, p. 222): the lattices
$\sigma L$ with $\sigma \in O(V)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82C, p. 222 (the class cls L)"]
def cls (L : Submodule R V) : Set (Submodule R V) :=
  {K | ∃ σ ∈ orth Q, K = latMap σ L}

/-- **Isometric lattices** $L \cong K$ (O'Meara 1963, §82A, p. 220): an $R$-linear bijection
$f : L \to K$ with $Q(f x) = Q(x)$; the lattices may lie in different quadratic spaces $(V, Q)$ and
$(V', Q')$. (O'Meara's isometry of $L$ onto $K$ is a linear isometry of $FL$ onto $FK$ carrying $L$ onto $K$; it is
determined by its restriction to $L$.) -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82A, p. 220 (isometry of lattices)"]
def IsometricLat {V' : Type*} [AddCommGroup V'] [Module F V'] [Module R V'] [IsScalarTower R F V']
    (Q' : QuadraticForm F V') (L : Submodule R V) (K : Submodule R V') : Prop :=
  ∃ f : L ≃ₗ[R] K, ∀ x : L, Q' (f x : V') = Q (x : V)

end Defs

/-! ### Basic properties of the bilinear form, the scale and the norm -/

section Basic

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra R F] [Invertible (2 : F)]
variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [Module R V] [IsScalarTower R F V]
variable (Q : QuadraticForm F V)

@[simp] theorem bil_self (x : V) : bil Q x x = Q x :=
  QuadraticMap.associated_eq_self_apply F Q x

theorem bil_comm (x y : V) : bil Q x y = bil Q y x :=
  QuadraticMap.associated_isSymm F Q x y

theorem bil_add_left (x x' y : V) : bil Q (x + x') y = bil Q x y + bil Q x' y := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_add_right (x y y' : V) : bil Q x (y + y') = bil Q x y + bil Q x y' := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_sub_left (x x' y : V) : bil Q (x - x') y = bil Q x y - bil Q x' y := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_sub_right (x y y' : V) : bil Q x (y - y') = bil Q x y - bil Q x y' := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_neg_left (x y : V) : bil Q (-x) y = -bil Q x y := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_smul_left (c : F) (x y : V) : bil Q (c • x) y = c * bil Q x y := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_smul_right (c : F) (x y : V) : bil Q x (c • y) = c * bil Q x y := by
  simp [bil]

theorem bil_rsmul_left (c : R) (x y : V) : bil Q (c • x) y = algebraMap R F c * bil Q x y := by
  rw [← algebraMap_smul F c x, bil_smul_left]

theorem bil_rsmul_right (c : R) (x y : V) : bil Q x (c • y) = algebraMap R F c * bil Q x y := by
  rw [← algebraMap_smul F c y, bil_smul_right]

theorem bil_sum_left {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (x : ι → V) (y : V) :
    bil Q (∑ i ∈ s, x i) y = ∑ i ∈ s, bil Q (x i) y := by
  simp [bil, map_sum, LinearMap.sum_apply]

theorem bil_sum_right {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (x : V) (y : ι → V) :
    bil Q x (∑ i ∈ s, y i) = ∑ i ∈ s, bil Q x (y i) := by
  simp [bil, map_sum]

/-- $Q(x + y) = Q(x) + 2B(x, y) + Q(y)$. -/
theorem Q_add (x y : V) : Q (x + y) = Q x + 2 * bil Q x y + Q y := by
  rw [← bil_self Q (x + y), bil_add_left, bil_add_right, bil_add_right, bil_self, bil_self,
    bil_comm Q y x]
  ring

theorem Q_smul (c : F) (x : V) : Q (c • x) = c ^ 2 * Q x := by
  rw [QuadraticMap.map_smul, smul_eq_mul, _root_.sq]

theorem Q_rsmul (c : R) (x : V) : Q (c • x) = algebraMap R F c ^ 2 * Q x := by
  rw [← algebraMap_smul F c x, Q_smul]

theorem bil_mem_scale {L : Submodule R V} {x y : V} (hx : x ∈ L) (hy : y ∈ L) : bil Q x y ∈ scale Q L :=
  subset_span ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩

theorem Q_mem_normIdeal {L : Submodule R V} {x : V} (hx : x ∈ L) : Q x ∈ normIdeal Q L :=
  subset_span ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- $\mathfrak nL \subseteq \mathfrak sL$ (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 227), since $Q(x) = B(x, x)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 227 (2sL ⊆ nL ⊆ sL)"]
theorem normIdeal_le_scale (L : Submodule R V) : normIdeal Q L ≤ scale Q L := by
  rw [normIdeal, span_le]
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  rw [← bil_self]; exact bil_mem_scale Q hx hx

/-- $2\,\mathfrak sL \subseteq \mathfrak nL$ (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 227), since
$2B(x, y) = Q(x + y) - Q(x) - Q(y)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 227 (2sL ⊆ nL ⊆ sL)"]
theorem two_mul_mem_normIdeal {L : Submodule R V} {c : F} (hc : c ∈ scale Q L) :
    2 * c ∈ normIdeal Q L := by
  refine span_induction (p := fun c _ => 2 * c ∈ normIdeal Q L) ?_ (by simp) ?_ ?_ hc
  · rintro _ ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩
    have h := Q_add Q x y
    have : 2 * bil Q x y = Q (x + y) - Q x - Q y := by rw [h]; ring
    rw [this]
    exact sub_mem (sub_mem (Q_mem_normIdeal Q (L.add_mem hx hy)) (Q_mem_normIdeal Q hx))
      (Q_mem_normIdeal Q hy)
  · intro a b _ _ ha hb
    rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem ha hb
  · intro r a _ ha
    rw [mul_smul_comm]; exact (normIdeal Q L).smul_mem r ha

theorem scale_mono {L K : Submodule R V} (h : L ≤ K) : scale Q L ≤ scale Q K :=
  span_mono (Set.image2_subset h h)

theorem normIdeal_mono {L K : Submodule R V} (h : L ≤ K) : normIdeal Q L ≤ normIdeal Q K :=
  span_mono (Set.image_mono h)

/-- **Scale from a spanning family** (O'Meara 1963, 82:8 (1), p. 227, with all $\mathfrak a_i = \mathfrak o$):
if $L = \sum_i R z_i$ then $\mathfrak sL = \sum_{i,j} R\,B(z_i, z_j)$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, 82:8 (1), p. 227"]
theorem scale_span {ι : Type*} (z : ι → V) :
    scale Q (span R (Set.range z)) = span R (Set.range fun p : ι × ι => bil Q (z p.1) (z p.2)) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [scale, span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩
    refine span_induction (p := fun x _ => bil Q x y ∈ span R _) ?_ (by simp [bil]) ?_ ?_ hx
    · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
      refine span_induction (p := fun y _ => bil Q (z i) y ∈ span R _) ?_ (by simp [bil]) ?_ ?_ hy
      · rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
        exact subset_span ⟨(i, j), rfl⟩
      · intro a b _ _ ha hb
        rw [bil_add_right]; exact add_mem ha hb
      · intro r a _ ha
        rw [bil_rsmul_right, ← Algebra.smul_def]; exact smul_mem _ r ha
    · intro a b _ _ ha hb
      rw [bil_add_left]; exact add_mem ha hb
    · intro r a _ ha
      rw [bil_rsmul_left, ← Algebra.smul_def]; exact smul_mem _ r ha
  · rw [span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
    exact bil_mem_scale Q (subset_span ⟨p.1, rfl⟩) (subset_span ⟨p.2, rfl⟩)

theorem scale_bot : scale Q (⊥ : Submodule R V) = ⊥ := by
  rw [scale, span_eq_bot]
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Submodule.mem_bot] at hx hy
  simp [hx, bil]

end Basic

/-! ### Lattices over a domain with fraction field $F$: bases, volume, modular lattices -/

section Domain

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra R F] [IsFractionRing R F]
  [Invertible (2 : F)]
variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [Module R V] [IsScalarTower R F V]
variable (Q : QuadraticForm F V)

omit [Invertible (2 : F)] in
include F in
/-- A vector space over the fraction field $F$ of $R$ is torsion-free over $R$. -/
theorem isTorsionFree_of_fractionRing : Module.IsTorsionFree R V := by
  refine Module.IsTorsionFree.of_smul_eq_zero fun r x h => ?_
  rw [← algebraMap_smul F r x, smul_eq_zero] at h
  rcases h with h | h
  · left
    exact (IsFractionRing.injective R F) (by simpa using h)
  · right; exact h

omit [Invertible (2 : F)] in
/-- If $x \in FS$ for an $R$-submodule $S \subseteq V$, then $d x \in S$ for some non-zero $d \in R$. -/
theorem exists_smul_mem_of_mem_span {S : Submodule R V} {x : V} (hx : x ∈ span F (S : Set V)) :
    ∃ d : R, d ≠ 0 ∧ d • x ∈ S := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy, z, rfl⟩ := (IsLocalization.mem_span_iff (nonZeroDivisors R) (S := F)).mp hx
  refine ⟨z, nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero z.2, ?_⟩
  rw [span_eq] at hy
  have : (z : R) • (IsLocalization.mk' F (1 : R) z • y) = y := by
    rw [← algebraMap_smul F (z : R), smul_smul, IsLocalization.mk'_spec'_mk, map_one, one_smul]
  rw [this]; exact hy

/-- The matrix of a family $x_i = \sum_j T_{ij} b_j$ (coefficients in $R$) is $T\,G\,T^{\mathsf T}$, where $G$ is
the matrix of $b$ (O'Meara 1963, §82B, p. 221: $N' = {}^tTNT$). -/
theorem gram_comb {ι κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (b : κ → V) (T : Matrix ι κ R) :
    gram Q (fun i => ∑ j, T i j • b j) =
      T.map (algebraMap R F) * gram Q b * (T.map (algebraMap R F))ᵀ := by
  ext i k
  simp only [gram, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.map_apply, Matrix.transpose_apply,
    bil_sum_left, bil_sum_right, bil_rsmul_left, bil_rsmul_right, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  ring

/-- **The volume from a base** (O'Meara 1963, §82E, p. 229): if $b$ is a base of $L$ then
$\mathfrak vL = d(b)\,R$ with $d(b) = \det(B(b_i, b_j))$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82E, p. 229 (vL = d(x₁,…,x_r) for a base)"]
theorem volume_eq_span_det {L : Submodule R V} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (b : Basis ι R L) : volume Q L = span R {(gram Q fun i => (b i : V)).det} := by
  have hr : finrank R L = Fintype.card ι := finrank_eq_card_basis b
  let e : Fin (finrank R L) ≃ ι := (Fintype.equivFinOfCardEq hr.symm).symm
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [volume, span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    -- coordinates of the `x i` in the base `b`
    let T : Matrix (Fin (finrank R L)) ι R := fun i j => b.repr ⟨x i, hx i⟩ j
    have hxT : x = fun i => ∑ j, T i j • (b j : V) := by
      funext i
      have := b.sum_repr ⟨x i, hx i⟩
      have h2 := congrArg Subtype.val this
      simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul] at h2
      exact h2.symm
    rw [hxT, gram_comb]
    -- reindex `T` to a square matrix
    let T' : Matrix ι ι R := Matrix.reindex e (Equiv.refl ι) T
    have hT : T.map (algebraMap R F) =
        (Matrix.reindex e.symm (Equiv.refl ι)) (T'.map (algebraMap R F)) := by
      ext i j; simp [T']
    rw [hT]
    have hdet : ((Matrix.reindex e.symm (Equiv.refl ι)) (T'.map (algebraMap R F)) * gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) *
        ((Matrix.reindex e.symm (Equiv.refl ι)) (T'.map (algebraMap R F)))ᵀ).det =
        (T'.map (algebraMap R F) * gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) * (T'.map (algebraMap R F))ᵀ).det := by
      rw [← Matrix.det_reindex_self e]
      congr 1
      ext i j
      simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.reindex_apply, Matrix.submatrix_apply]
    rw [hdet, Matrix.det_mul, Matrix.det_mul, Matrix.det_transpose,
      show (T'.map (algebraMap R F)).det = algebraMap R F T'.det from (RingHom.map_det _ _).symm]
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, mem_span_singleton]
    exact ⟨T'.det * T'.det, by rw [Algebra.smul_def]; simp; ring⟩
  · rw [span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    refine subset_span ⟨fun i => (b (e i) : V), fun i => (b (e i)).2, ?_⟩
    have : gram Q (fun i => (b (e i) : V)) = Matrix.reindex e.symm e.symm (gram Q fun i => (b i : V)) := by
      ext i j; simp [gram]
    rw [this, Matrix.det_reindex_self]

/-- The vectors of a base of $L$ span $L$. -/
theorem span_basis_eq {L : Submodule R V} {ι : Type*} (b : Basis ι R L) :
    span R (Set.range fun i => (b i : V)) = L := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [span_le]; rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact (b i).2
  · intro x hx
    have h1 : (⟨x, hx⟩ : L) ∈ span R (Set.range b) := b.span_eq ▸ mem_top
    have h2 := Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (f := L.subtype) h1
    rw [Submodule.map_span, ← Set.range_comp] at h2
    exact h2

/-- **Modular lattices in a base** (O'Meara 1963, 82:13, p. 231, for an arbitrary scale $\alpha R$): a lattice $L$
with base $b$ is $\alpha$-modular ($\alpha \ne 0$) if and only if $L \ne 0$ and its matrix is
$(B(b_i, b_j)) = \alpha U$ with $U$ an invertible matrix over $R$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, 82:13, p. 231 (for the scale αo)"]
theorem isModular_iff_gram {L : Submodule R V} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (b : Basis ι R L)
    {α : F} (hα : α ≠ 0) :
    IsModular Q (R ∙ α) L ↔ Nonempty ι ∧ ∃ U : Matrix ι ι R, IsUnit U.det ∧
      gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) = α • U.map (algebraMap R F) := by
  have hr : finrank R L = Fintype.card ι := finrank_eq_card_basis b
  have hsc : scale Q L = span R (Set.range fun p : ι × ι => bil Q (b p.1 : V) (b p.2 : V)) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← span_basis_eq b]
    exact scale_span Q _
  have hpow : (R ∙ α) ^ finrank R L = R ∙ α ^ Fintype.card ι := by
    rw [span_pow, Set.singleton_pow, hr]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨-, hs, hv⟩
    -- the entries `B(b_i, b_j) / α` are integral
    have hent : ∀ i j, ∃ u : R, u • α = bil Q (b i : V) (b j : V) := fun i j => by
      have : bil Q (b i : V) (b j : V) ∈ R ∙ α := hs ▸ bil_mem_scale Q (b i).2 (b j).2
      exact mem_span_singleton.mp this
    choose U hU using hent
    have hG : gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) = α • (Matrix.of U).map (algebraMap R F) := by
      ext i j; simp [gram, ← hU i j, Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm]
    have hne : Nonempty ι := by
      by_contra h
      rw [not_nonempty_iff] at h
      have : scale Q L = ⊥ := by
        rw [hsc, span_eq_bot]; rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩; exact (IsEmpty.false p.1).elim
      rw [this] at hs
      exact hα ((span_singleton_eq_bot).mp hs.symm)
    refine ⟨hne, Matrix.of U, ?_, hG⟩
    rw [volume_eq_span_det Q b, hG, hpow, Matrix.det_smul,
      show ((Matrix.of U).map (algebraMap R F)).det = algebraMap R F (Matrix.of U).det from
        (RingHom.map_det _ _).symm] at hv
    -- `α^r det U` generates `α^r R`, so `det U` is a unit
    have hαr : α ^ Fintype.card ι ≠ 0 := pow_ne_zero _ hα
    have h1 : α ^ Fintype.card ι ∈ R ∙ (α ^ Fintype.card ι * algebraMap R F (Matrix.of U).det) := by
      rw [hv]; exact mem_span_singleton_self _
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := mem_span_singleton.mp h1
    rw [Algebra.smul_def] at hc
    have : algebraMap R F (c * (Matrix.of U).det) = algebraMap R F 1 := by
      rw [map_mul, map_one]
      apply mul_left_cancel₀ hαr
      linear_combination hc
    exact IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one_right c (IsFractionRing.injective R F this)
  · rintro ⟨hne, U, hU, hG⟩
    refine ⟨by simpa using hα, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [hsc]
      apply le_antisymm
      · rw [span_le]
        rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
        change bil Q (b p.1 : V) (b p.2 : V) ∈ (R ∙ α)
        have : bil Q (b p.1 : V) (b p.2 : V) = U p.1 p.2 • α := by
          have := congrFun (congrFun hG p.1) p.2
          simp only [gram, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.map_apply, smul_eq_mul] at this
          rw [this, Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm]
        rw [this]; exact smul_mem _ _ (mem_span_singleton_self α)
      · -- `det U` lies in the ideal generated by the entries of `U`, so `1` does
        rw [span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
        obtain ⟨i⟩ := hne
        have hdet : U.det = ∑ j, U i j * U.adjugate j i := by
          have := congrFun (congrFun (Matrix.mul_adjugate U) i) i
          simpa [Matrix.mul_apply] using this.symm
        obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hU.exists_left_inv
        have hb : ∀ j, bil Q (b i : V) (b j : V) = algebraMap R F (U i j) * α := fun j => by
          have := congrFun (congrFun hG i) j
          simp only [gram, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.map_apply, smul_eq_mul] at this
          rw [this, mul_comm]
        have hsum : ∑ j, v * U.adjugate j i * U i j = 1 := by
          rw [← hv, hdet, Finset.mul_sum]
          refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
          ring
        have : α = ∑ j, (v * U.adjugate j i) • bil Q (b i : V) (b j : V) := by
          simp only [hb, Algebra.smul_def]
          calc α = algebraMap R F (∑ j, v * U.adjugate j i * U i j) * α := by
                rw [hsum, map_one, one_mul]
            _ = _ := by
                rw [map_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
                refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
                rw [map_mul, map_mul]; ring
        rw [this]
        exact sum_mem fun j _ => smul_mem _ _ (subset_span ⟨(i, j), rfl⟩)
    · rw [volume_eq_span_det Q b, hG, hpow, Matrix.det_smul,
        show (U.map (algebraMap R F)).det = algebraMap R F U.det from (RingHom.map_det _ _).symm]
      obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hU
      rw [← hu, mul_comm, ← Algebra.smul_def, Submodule.span_singleton_smul_eq u.isUnit]


/-- A vector $x$ whose products $B(x, b_j)$ with a base $b$ of an $\alpha$-modular lattice $J$ lie in $\alpha R$
has the same products with $J$ as some $y \in J$ (the key step of 82:14a and 82:15). Here the matrix of $J$ is
$\alpha U$ with $U$ invertible over $R$. -/
theorem exists_mem_bil_eq_of_gram {J : Submodule R V} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (b : Basis ι R J) {α : F} {U : Matrix ι ι R} (hU : IsUnit U.det)
    (hG : gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) = α • U.map (algebraMap R F)) {x : V}
    (hx : ∀ j, bil Q x (b j : V) ∈ R ∙ α) : ∃ y ∈ J, ∀ z ∈ J, bil Q y z = bil Q x z := by
  choose w hw using fun j => mem_span_singleton.mp (hx j)
  let c : ι → R := Matrix.vecMul w U⁻¹
  refine ⟨∑ i, c i • (b i : V), sum_mem fun i _ => J.smul_mem _ (b i).2, ?_⟩
  have hcU : Matrix.vecMul c U = w := by
    simp only [c, Matrix.vecMul_vecMul, Matrix.nonsing_inv_mul _ hU, Matrix.vecMul_one]
  have hbase : ∀ k, bil Q (∑ i, c i • (b i : V)) (b k : V) = bil Q x (b k : V) := by
    intro k
    rw [← hw k, bil_sum_left]
    simp only [bil_rsmul_left]
    have hGk : ∀ i, bil Q (b i : V) (b k : V) = α * algebraMap R F (U i k) := fun i => by
      have := congrFun (congrFun hG i) k
      simpa [gram] using this
    simp only [hGk]
    have : w k = ∑ i, c i * U i k := by rw [← hcU]; rfl
    rw [this, Algebra.smul_def, map_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [map_mul]; ring
  intro z hz
  rw [← span_basis_eq b] at hz
  refine span_induction (p := fun z _ => bil Q (∑ i, c i • (b i : V)) z = bil Q x z) ?_ (by simp [bil])
    ?_ ?_ hz
  · rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩; exact hbase k
  · intro z z' _ _ h h'; rw [bil_add_right, bil_add_right, h, h']
  · intro r z _ h; rw [bil_rsmul_right, bil_rsmul_right, h]

/-- A lattice whose matrix in a base is $\alpha U$ with $\alpha \ne 0$ and $U$ invertible is regular. -/
theorem isRegular_of_gram {J : Submodule R V} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (b : Basis ι R J) {α : F} (hα : α ≠ 0) {U : Matrix ι ι R} (hU : IsUnit U.det)
    (hG : gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) = α • U.map (algebraMap R F)) : IsRegular Q J := by
  intro x hx h0
  let c : ι → R := b.repr ⟨x, hx⟩
  have hxc : x = ∑ i, c i • (b i : V) := by
    have := b.sum_repr ⟨x, hx⟩
    have h2 := congrArg Subtype.val this
    simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul] at h2
    exact h2.symm
  have hcU : Matrix.vecMul c U = 0 := by
    funext k
    have h1 := h0 (b k) (b k).2
    rw [hxc, bil_sum_left] at h1
    simp only [bil_rsmul_left] at h1
    have hGk : ∀ i, bil Q (b i : V) (b k : V) = α * algebraMap R F (U i k) := fun i => by
      have := congrFun (congrFun hG i) k
      simpa [gram] using this
    simp only [hGk] at h1
    have : algebraMap R F (Matrix.vecMul c U k) = 0 := by
      have h2 : α * algebraMap R F (Matrix.vecMul c U k) = 0 := by
        rw [← h1, Matrix.vecMul, dotProduct, map_sum, Finset.mul_sum]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        rw [map_mul]; ring
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp h2).resolve_left hα
    simpa using (IsFractionRing.injective R F) (this.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  have hc : c = 0 := by
    have := congrArg (fun v => Matrix.vecMul v U⁻¹) hcU
    simpa [Matrix.vecMul_vecMul, Matrix.mul_nonsing_inv _ hU] using this
  rw [hxc, hc]; simp

end Domain

/-! ### Lattices over a discrete valuation ring -/

section DVR

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra R F] [IsFractionRing R F] [Invertible (2 : F)]
variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [Module R V] [IsScalarTower R F V]
variable (Q : QuadraticForm F V)

omit [Invertible (2 : F)] in
include F in
/-- **Every lattice over a discrete valuation ring is free** (O'Meara 1963, Chapter IX, p. 239: "every non-zero
lattice is free"; here from Mathlib's structure theorem over a principal ideal domain). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "Chapter IX, p. 239 (every lattice is free)"]
theorem exists_basis {L : Submodule R V} (hL : L.FG) : Nonempty (Basis (Fin (finrank R L)) R L) := by
  have := isTorsionFree_of_fractionRing (R := R) (F := F) (V := V)
  have : Module.Finite R L := Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr hL
  have : Module.Free R L := Module.free_of_finite_type_torsion_free'
  exact ⟨Module.finBasis R L⟩

omit [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] [Invertible (2 : F)] in
/-- In a valuation ring, of two elements of $F$ one divides the other. -/
theorem span_pair_eq [IsDomain R] [ValuationRing R] (a b : F) :
    (R ∙ a) ⊔ (R ∙ b) = R ∙ a ∨ (R ∙ a) ⊔ (R ∙ b) = R ∙ b := by
  by_cases ha : a = 0
  · right; simp [ha]
  by_cases hb : b = 0
  · left; simp [hb]
  rcases ValuationRing.isInteger_or_isInteger R (b / a) with ⟨r, hr⟩ | ⟨r, hr⟩
  · left
    have : b ∈ R ∙ a := mem_span_singleton.mpr ⟨r, by rw [Algebra.smul_def, hr, div_mul_cancel₀ _ ha]⟩
    exact sup_eq_left.mpr ((span_singleton_le_iff_mem _ _).mpr this)
  · right
    have : a ∈ R ∙ b := mem_span_singleton.mpr ⟨r, by
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, hr, inv_div, div_mul_cancel₀ _ hb]⟩
    exact sup_eq_right.mpr ((span_singleton_le_iff_mem _ _).mpr this)

omit [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] [Invertible (2 : F)] in
/-- **Finitely generated submodules of $F$ over a valuation ring are generated by one of the generators**
(O'Meara 1963, §91, pp. 239–240: "if we take ... $|B(x,y)|$ largest, then $B(L,L) = B(x,y)\mathfrak o$"). -/
theorem exists_mem_span_eq_singleton [IsDomain R] [ValuationRing R] {S : Set F} (hS : (span R S).FG) :
    ∃ a, (a ∈ S ∨ a = 0) ∧ span R S = R ∙ a := by
  obtain ⟨t, hts, hspan⟩ := (fg_span_iff_fg_span_finset_subset S).mp hS
  rw [hspan]
  clear hspan
  classical
  induction t using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => exact ⟨0, Or.inr rfl, by simp⟩
  | insert x t hx ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hta⟩ := ih (fun y hy => hts (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hy))
    have hxS : x ∈ S := hts (Finset.mem_insert_self x t)
    rw [Finset.coe_insert, span_insert, hta]
    rcases span_pair_eq (R := R) x a with h | h
    · exact ⟨x, Or.inl hxS, h⟩
    · exact ⟨a, ha, h⟩

omit [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] [IsFractionRing R F] in
/-- The scale of a finitely generated lattice is finitely generated. -/
theorem scale_fg {L : Submodule R V} (hL : L.FG) : (scale Q L).FG := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hL
  rw [← hs]
  have : span R (s : Set V) = span R (Set.range fun x : s => (x : V)) := by simp
  rw [this, scale_span]
  exact fg_span (Set.finite_range _)

/-- **The scale is attained** (O'Meara 1963, §91, p. 240): for a lattice $L$ there are $x, y \in L$ with
$\mathfrak sL = B(x, y)\,\mathfrak o$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§91, pp. 239–240 (sL = B(x,y)o for |B(x,y)| largest)"]
theorem exists_scale_eq {L : Submodule R V} (hL : L.FG) :
    ∃ x ∈ L, ∃ y ∈ L, scale Q L = R ∙ bil Q x y := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, h⟩ := exists_mem_span_eq_singleton (R := R) (scale_fg Q hL)
  rcases ha with ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩ | rfl
  · exact ⟨x, hx, y, hy, h⟩
  · exact ⟨0, L.zero_mem, 0, L.zero_mem, by rw [scale, h]; simp [bil]⟩

/-- **The norm is attained** (O'Meara 1963, §91, p. 240): for a lattice $L$ there is $x \in L$ with
$\mathfrak nL = Q(x)\,\mathfrak o$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§91, p. 240 (nL = Q(x)o for |Q(x)| largest)"]
theorem exists_normIdeal_eq {L : Submodule R V} (hL : L.FG) : ∃ x ∈ L, normIdeal Q L = R ∙ Q x := by
  have hfg : (normIdeal Q L).FG := FG.of_le (scale_fg Q hL) (normIdeal_le_scale Q L)
  obtain ⟨a, ha, h⟩ := exists_mem_span_eq_singleton (R := R) hfg
  rcases ha with ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ | rfl
  · exact ⟨x, hx, h⟩
  · exact ⟨0, L.zero_mem, by rw [normIdeal, h]; simp⟩

omit [Invertible (2 : F)] in
/-- A non-zero finitely generated $R$-submodule of $F$ is $\alpha R$ for some $\alpha \ne 0$ (every fractional
ideal of a local field is principal). -/
theorem exists_eq_span_singleton {a : Submodule R F} (ha : a.FG) (h0 : a ≠ ⊥) :
    ∃ α : F, α ≠ 0 ∧ a = R ∙ α := by
  obtain ⟨α, -, h⟩ := exists_mem_span_eq_singleton (R := R) (S := (a : Set F)) (by rwa [span_eq])
  rw [span_eq] at h
  refine ⟨α, ?_, h⟩
  rintro rfl; exact h0 (by simpa using h)

/-- A finitely generated $\mathfrak a$-modular lattice has $\mathfrak a = \alpha R$ and, in a base, the matrix
$\alpha U$ with $U$ invertible over $R$. -/
theorem exists_gram_of_isModular {a : Submodule R F} {J : Submodule R V} (hJ : IsModular Q a J)
    (hJfg : J.FG) : ∃ α : F, α ≠ 0 ∧ a = R ∙ α ∧ ∃ b : Basis (Fin (finrank R J)) R J,
      ∃ U : Matrix (Fin (finrank R J)) (Fin (finrank R J)) R, IsUnit U.det ∧
        gram Q (fun i => (b i : V)) = α • U.map (algebraMap R F) := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_span_singleton (R := R) (hJ.2.1 ▸ scale_fg Q hJfg) hJ.1
  obtain ⟨b⟩ := exists_basis (R := R) (F := F) hJfg
  obtain ⟨-, U, hU, hG⟩ := (isModular_iff_gram Q b hα).mp hJ
  exact ⟨α, hα, rfl, b, U, hU, hG⟩

/-- **A modular lattice is regular** (O'Meara 1963, §82G, p. 231). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, p. 231 (an a-modular lattice is regular)"]
theorem IsModular.isRegular {a : Submodule R F} {J : Submodule R V} (hJ : IsModular Q a J) (hJfg : J.FG) :
    IsRegular Q J := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα, -, b, U, hU, hG⟩ := exists_gram_of_isModular Q hJ hJfg
  exact isRegular_of_gram Q b hα hU hG

/-- **Splitting criterion** (O'Meara 1963, 82:15, p. 232): an $\mathfrak a$-modular sublattice $J$ of $L$ splits
$L$ (i.e. $L = J \perp K$ for some $K$) if and only if $B(J, L) \subseteq \mathfrak a$. The complement constructed
is $K = \{x \in L : B(x, J) = 0\}$ (`splitComp`). -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, 82:15, p. 232"]
theorem splits_iff_of_isModular {a : Submodule R F} {L J : Submodule R V} (hJL : J ≤ L)
    (hJ : IsModular Q a J) (hJfg : J.FG) :
    (∃ K, IsOrthSum Q L J K) ↔ ∀ x ∈ J, ∀ y ∈ L, bil Q x y ∈ a := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨K, hK⟩ x hx y hy
    rw [← hK.sup_eq] at hy
    obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁, y₂, hy₂, rfl⟩ := mem_sup.mp hy
    rw [bil_add_right, hK.orth x hx y₂ hy₂, add_zero, ← hJ.2.1]
    exact bil_mem_scale Q hx hy₁
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨α, hα, rfl, b, U, hU, hG⟩ := exists_gram_of_isModular Q hJ hJfg
    refine ⟨splitComp Q L J, ⟨fun _ hx _ hy => by rw [bil_comm]; exact hy.2 _ hx, ?_, ?_⟩⟩
    · rw [disjoint_iff, eq_bot_iff]
      rintro x ⟨hxJ, hxK⟩
      exact (mem_bot R).mpr (IsModular.isRegular Q hJ hJfg x hxJ fun y hy => hxK.2 y hy)
    · apply le_antisymm
      · exact sup_le hJL fun x hx => hx.1
      · intro x hx
        obtain ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩ := exists_mem_bil_eq_of_gram Q b hU hG (x := x) fun j => by
          rw [bil_comm]; exact h _ (b j).2 x hx
        refine mem_sup.mpr ⟨y, hy, x - y, ⟨L.sub_mem hx (hJL hy), fun z hz => ?_⟩, by abel⟩
        rw [bil_sub_left, hxy z hz, sub_self]

/-- **Corollary 82:15a** (O'Meara 1963, p. 233): an $\mathfrak a$-modular sublattice $J$ of a lattice $L$ with
$\mathfrak sL = \mathfrak a$ splits $L$. -/
@[kb "omeara1963" "§82G, 82:15a, p. 233"]
theorem splits_of_isModular_of_scale_eq {a : Submodule R F} {L J : Submodule R V} (hJL : J ≤ L)
    (hJ : IsModular Q a J) (hJfg : J.FG) (hL : scale Q L = a) : ∃ K, IsOrthSum Q L J K :=
  (splits_iff_of_isModular Q hJL hJ hJfg).mpr fun _ hx _ hy => hL ▸ bil_mem_scale Q (hJL hx) hy

end DVR

end QuadFormsKB.OMeara
